# cmd.exe misparses LF-only batch files (setup.bat exits immediately when
# downloaded from a source ZIP). Do not rely on archive-time attribute
# conversion: attributes never rewrite files already extracted to disk, and
# an archive generated before the attributes were committed keeps the old LF
# blobs. Store CRLF in the blob itself instead. `-text` disables all EOL
# conversion, so checkout, clone, ZIP and tarball downloads all get the exact
# CRLF bytes committed here. Keep these files CRLF when editing them.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
